The hand-written fixture. The expected values in fixture.go are counted by
hand from this table, not by the code under test.

Mail file                     Message  Sender                    Rule
allen-p/inbox/1.              M1       phillip.allen@enron.com   Copy in several folders and mailboxes
allen-p/all_documents/1.      M1       phillip.allen@enron.com   Copy, own Message-ID
bass-e/inbox/1.               M1       phillip.allen@enron.com   Copy in another mailbox
allen-p/sent/2.               M2       phillip.allen@enron.com   From differs only in case and whitespace
bass-e/sent/1.                M3       eric.bass@enron.com       Copy, LF line endings
bass-e/sent_items/1.          M3       eric.bass@enron.com       Copy, CRLF and whitespace-only body changes
bass-e/inbox/2.               M4       eric.bass@enron.com       identical header fields to M5
bass-e/inbox/3.               M5       eric.bass@enron.com       identical header fields to M4, other body
lay-k/inbox/1.                M6       (none)                    From with no @: a Message without a Sender
lay-k/inbox/2.                M7       john..doe@enron.com       From the strict parser rejects: recovered
lay-k/sent/1.                 M8       kenneth.lay@enron.com     To with mixed case and a duplicate
skilling-j/inbox/1.           M9       jeff.skilling@enron.com   folded Subject: unfolded
kean-s/inbox/1.               M10      steven.kean@enron.com     colon-less header line: skipped
kean-s/inbox/2.               M11      steven.kean@enron.com     no empty line: all header, empty body
skilling-j/inbox/2.           M12      sally.beck@enron.com      RFC 2047 Subject in UTF-8: decoded
skilling-j/inbox/3.           M13      vince.kaminski@enron.com  RFC 2047 Subject in ISO-8859-1: decoded
skilling-j/inbox/4.           M14      mark.taylor@enron.com     RFC 2047 Subject in KOI8-R: kept as written
skilling-j/inbox/5.           M15      scott.neal@enron.com      RFC 2047 Subject in ANSI_X3.4-1968, an alias: decoded
skilling-j/inbox/6.           M16      susan.scott@enron.com     RFC 2047 word with no charset: kept as written
kean-s/inbox/3.               M17      louise.kitchen@enron.com  non-UTF-8 byte in the Subject
lay-k/inbox/3.                M18      greg.whalley@enron.com    the 1979 placeholder Date
kean-s/sent/1.                M19      richard.shapiro@enron.com Bcc copies Cc

22 Mail files, 19 Messages, 14 Senders, 1 Message without a Sender.

Top Senders: eric.bass 3; phillip.allen 2, steven.kean 2; then the senders
with 1, by address: greg.whalley, jeff.skilling, john..doe, kenneth.lay,
louise.kitchen, mark.taylor, richard.shapiro. sally.beck, scott.neal,
susan.scott and vince.kaminski also have 1: the tie at the 10th and 11th
place goes to richard.shapiro by address.
